From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:58:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] vulkan: 2-row MMVQ for Q5_K / IQ4_XS above four columns
 on RDNA3/4; Qwen3.8-27B verify-shape tests

- Q5_K and IQ4_XS integer-dot matvec use 2 rows per workgroup from 5 columns on (other types keep 4).
  Cold weights, Radeon 8060S (gfx1151), n=5: q5_K m=17408 k=5120 351 -> 334 us, iq4_xs 286 -> 272 us,
  q5_K m=6144 k=5120 143 -> 135 us. Qwen3.8-27B MTP + 64K draft vocabulary, same session: n4 chat
  31.1 -> 31.6, code 36.0 -> 36.6, 32K 25.9 -> 26.3; n5 code 37.2 -> 38.0 tok/s. Greedy outputs are
  identical with and without.
- GGML_VK_DMMV_LARGE_MAX_M / _MIN_K / _FORCE: experiment knobs for the AMD large-workgroup matvec (the GLM
  series 0018 rule with 1024 / 8192), off by default: the large workgroup reduces in a different order,
  and it gave nothing at these shapes.
- test-backend-ops: test_mul_mat_cold with Qwen3.8-27B decode/verify shapes at n=1..8 (eval) and
  cold-weight perf variants (nw distinct weights beyond the 32 MiB MALL; us/run / nw per matvec).

Tried, not kept: an A-load-once multi-column MMVQ path for Q4_K / Q5_K / IQ4_XS (no gain; the compiler
already shares the A loads across columns).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
